            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0382" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/14505: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-08-29T14:00:00+01:00">August 29, 1941—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 29—9:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3962. Reference to the Department’s 3375, August 25, 5 p.m., 3376 August 25, 6
                    p.m., 3377 August 25, 7 p.m. I have discussed statement quoted in 3376 August
                    25, 6 p.m. with both Mr. Churchill and Mr. Eden. The Prime Minister asked for
                    time to consult with other members of the Cabinet before giving me a final
                    answer. I told him that of course we understood his obligation to do that. He
                    himself seemed to favor making the statement and is certainly in sympathy with
                    the underlying principles on which it is based.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
